geraldine uriel needed the equivalent of  500 euros to buy this dairy cow  a normal bank would never have approved  a loan but thanks to 36  investors from around the world she  raised the money  now she earns a living selling her cow's  milk and has already paid off her debts  she recently organized a second micro  credit  i took out a loan of 100 000 kenyan  shillings and used it to buy 250  chickens  in two weeks time they'll start laying  eggs then i can sell them  and earn about 2 000 shillings a week  the business that facilitated her loan  is based in the kenyan capital nairobi  mad kier from denmark launched the  online social lending platform  my c4 in 2006.  it matches people who have money with  those who need it  on friday but this one is actually too  high so it's 100 funded  how my c4 works is that there's a  competition between the lenders  about what interest rate they will bid  in principle you can lend your money out  at zero percent interest  then you don't earn anything but you can  relent it and re-lend it when you're  getting repaid  but you could also choose an interest  rate do you want to make money or you're  a social investor or maybe you're both  mad kier sees himself as a social  entrepreneur  but he also has his eye on the bottom  line one third of the interest on the  loans goes to my c4  for now kiara partly funds his business  out of his own pocket  he runs the care group set up by his  father  yes we lent about 4 million  euros out in 2013 and that paid half of  our costs  so if we can double that to 8 million  euro it will pay all of our cost and we  will be a business making a profit  so that's target 1 target 2 is to grow  much more  i mean you have more than 100 million  people living in kenya uganda and  tanzania that's a huge market  today kiara is on his way to kiambu 20  kilometers north of nairobi  he's meeting one of my c4's local  partners  their input is valuable to the business  they know many of the platforms users  personally  in the early days the business saw heavy  losses  but madskyr has learned from the  mistakes  that was one of the reasons why we  failed yes we did it from denmark  so that was of course also extremely  expensive that we had to fly down and  you know stay in hotels and  uh didn't make any sense and we didn't  have the local knowledge like eric and  kevin and the team has  together with daniel kimani who heads  the regional office  he's developing a further aspect of the  company  the plan is to allow lenders to invest  not just in individuals but also in  groups  for every loan that we are coming to  land it must have been approved by the  group  the group must have given a guarantee  remember this group  for them to be assessed to be ready for  wrongs they must also show  ability to raise some retro money of  their own which they manage on their own  these funds it is correctively agreed  within the group  they would be used to help any of their  members  if they are struggling to pay the loans  380 million people in africa have no  bank account  that means they can't get loans  peter lawrence is one of them but now  he's the owner of three offices for  mobile money transfers  his loan is guaranteed by a group  as far as mods care is concerned he's a  model entrepreneur  it's doing great i have a quite good  turn up of the customers under the  challenges i'm able to meet  to compare challenges with some  intervention that i'm doing some  strategies like  customer service i'm being late peter  you know i've been working 30 years in  africa  and why we created myc4 and the  partnership was with keith  was to fund businesses like you so you  could grow yeah because the banks  doesn't want to go there and you  you want to borrow more than a  microfinance institution normally lend  out  yeah and they want to collateralize  everything yeah and you actually don't  have that  yeah but you have a group and that makes  me very proud to see how you're growing  back 